<% content_for :title, "Privacy Policy · BiblioRata" %>
<div class="ps-root ps-tut-root">
  <div class="ps-tut">
    <header class="ps-tut-hero">
      <div class="eyebrow">&#9769; &nbsp; BiblioRata &nbsp; &#9769;</div>
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="lede">Last updated: <%= LegalController::PRIVACY_UPDATED_ON.to_fs(:long) %></p>
      <div class="ps-tut-hero-cta">
        <%= link_to "Back to your desk", root_path, class: "cta secondary" %>
        <%= link_to "Terms of Service", terms_path, class: "cta secondary" %>
      </div>
    </header>

    <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 pb-16 text-[17px] leading-relaxed">
      <p>BiblioRata (&ldquo;we&rdquo;, &ldquo;us&rdquo;) is a Bible reading, study and preaching
         app. This policy covers the website at bibliorata.com and the BiblioRata apps for Android
         and iPhone, which show the same service. We collect only what the app needs to work, we
         never sell your data, and we don&rsquo;t show ads.</p>

      <h2 class="mt-8 mb-2 text-xl font-semibold">1. What we collect</h2>
      <p>You can read the Bible, compare translations and use most study tools without an account.
         If you create one, we store:</p>
      <ul class="ml-6 list-disc">
        <li><strong>Account:</strong> your email address and your password, stored only as a
            secure hash (we never see the password itself), plus your display preferences such as
            theme and text size.</li>
        <li><strong>Your study content:</strong> studies, the passages open in them, notes,
            highlights and highlight notes, reading plans and the days you finish, plan
            reflections, and preach queues (songs, thoughts and any pictures you upload for
            them).</li>
        <li><strong>Sign-in sessions:</strong> the IP address and browser or app version of each
            sign-in, so you stay signed in. Sessions expire after 30 days.</li>
        <li><strong>Testimonials:</strong> if you choose to leave a testimonial or a rating, we
            store what you write. If we publish a testimonial on our home page, it is shown with the
            part of your email address before the &ldquo;@&rdquo;.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="mt-4">Without an account, a study you work on is kept on our server and linked
         to your browser or app by a cookie.</p>
      <p class="mt-4">Information collected automatically:</p>
      <ul class="ml-6 list-disc">
        <li><strong>Server logs:</strong> your IP address, browser or app version and the pages you
            request, kept for security and troubleshooting. The text of your notes and of your AI
            questions is filtered out of these logs.</li>
        <li><strong>Error reports:</strong> when something breaks, a technical report of the
            error may be sent to our error-monitoring service. We configure it not to include your
            email address, IP address, cookies or what you typed.</li>
        <li><strong>On your device:</strong> Bibles you download for offline reading, and
            settings such as your theme, are stored in your browser or app on your device.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="mt-4">We do not use advertising, analytics or tracking tools, and we don&rsquo;t
         collect your location, contacts, photos library, microphone or camera. The only pictures
         we receive are ones you choose to upload.</p>

      <h2 class="mt-8 mb-2 text-xl font-semibold">2. How we use it</h2>
      <ul class="ml-6 list-disc">
        <li>To provide the app: save your studies, notes, highlights and plans and show them on
            every device you sign in on.</li>
        <li>To run the features you ask for, such as AI study help, audio Bible, sharing and
            live follow-along.</li>
        <li>To send you emails you request, such as a password reset.</li>
        <li>To keep the service secure, prevent abuse and fix problems.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="mt-8 mb-2 text-xl font-semibold">3. AI features</h2>
      <p>The AI tools (the Rabbi, Find a Verse, quick search, chapter prayers, diagrams and
         illustrations) need an account. When you use one, the passage you selected, the
         surrounding chapter and the text you typed are sent to an AI provider (Google Gemini,
         OpenAI or Abacus.AI) to produce the answer. Some answers are cached so a repeated question
         doesn&rsquo;t need another call. Please don&rsquo;t put personal or confidential
         information into AI questions.</p>

      <h2 class="mt-8 mb-2 text-xl font-semibold">4. What others can see</h2>
      <p>Your studies, notes and highlights are private to you. Some things become visible to
         others only when you choose: a study you share by link, a passage or prayer you share, and
         a live session you start (anyone with the link or QR code can follow it). A published
         testimonial is visible on our home page.</p>

      <h2 class="mt-8 mb-2 text-xl font-semibold">5. Who we share it with</h2>
      <p>We don&rsquo;t sell or rent your data and we don&rsquo;t share it for advertising. We use
         these service providers to run BiblioRata, and each gets only what it needs:</p>
      <ul class="ml-6 list-disc">
        <li><strong>Hosting and security:</strong> our servers and database (Hetzner, in the EU),
            and Cloudflare, which protects and speeds up the site.</li>
        <li><strong>Image storage:</strong> Cloudinary stores pictures you upload to a preach
            queue.</li>
        <li><strong>AI providers:</strong> Google, OpenAI and Abacus.AI, as described above. Google
            and OpenAI also turn Scripture text into speech for the audio Bible; no personal data is
            sent for that.</li>
        <li><strong>Email:</strong> an email delivery provider sends password-reset emails.</li>
        <li><strong>Error monitoring:</strong> Sentry, for the error reports described above.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="mt-4">We may also disclose information if the law requires it, or to protect
         someone&rsquo;s safety.</p>

      <h2 class="mt-8 mb-2 text-xl font-semibold">6. Cookies</h2>
      <p>We use only cookies that the app needs: a session cookie, a sign-in cookie, a security
         token, and small preference cookies such as your reading theme. No advertising or tracking
         cookies.</p>

      <h2 class="mt-8 mb-2 text-xl font-semibold">7. Your choices and rights</h2>
      <ul class="ml-6 list-disc">
        <li><strong>Download your data:</strong> on the Account page, download every study, note,
            highlight and reading plan as a file.</li>
        <li><strong>Delete your account:</strong> in the app go to More &rarr; Account &rarr;
            Delete my account, or on the web at <%= link_to "bibliorata.com/account", account_url %>.
            This permanently deletes your account and everything in it.
            <%= link_to "How to delete your account", delete_account_path %> also explains how to ask
            us by email.</li>
        <li>You can contact us to access, correct or erase your data, or to object to how we use
            it. Depending on where you live, you may also complain to your data-protection
            authority.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="mt-8 mb-2 text-xl font-semibold">8. How long we keep it</h2>
      <p>We keep your content while your account is open. When you delete your account, your
         studies, notes, highlights, reading plans, sign-in sessions, testimonials and uploaded
         pictures are deleted from our live systems straight away. Copies may remain in backups for
         a limited time until they are overwritten, and server logs are kept for a short period for
         security.</p>

      <h2 class="mt-8 mb-2 text-xl font-semibold">9. Security</h2>
      <p>All traffic is encrypted (HTTPS), passwords are stored only as secure hashes, and sign-in
         and other sensitive actions are rate-limited. No system is perfectly secure, so please use
         a strong, unique password. We will tell you about a breach affecting your data as the law
         requires.</p>

      <h2 class="mt-8 mb-2 text-xl font-semibold">10. Children</h2>
      <p>BiblioRata is not directed at children under 13, and children under 13 should not create
         an account. If you believe a child under 13 has an account, contact us and we will delete
         it.</p>

      <h2 class="mt-8 mb-2 text-xl font-semibold">11. Changes</h2>
      <p>If we change this policy, we will post the new version here and update the date above.
         For significant changes we will also let you know in the app.</p>

      <h2 class="mt-8 mb-2 text-xl font-semibold">12. Contact us</h2>
      <p>Questions or requests about your privacy: <%= mail_to LegalController.contact_email %>.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
</div>
